========================================================================
  PART 1: Tr(B^4) BY ROOT PAIR TYPE
========================================================================
  A_4 root pair inner products:
    <α,β> = -1: 10 pairs — ACUTE (-1)
    <α,β> = +0: 15 pairs — ORTHOGONAL (Petersen edge)
    <α,β> = +1: 20 pairs — OBTUSE (+1)

  Total root pairs: C(10,2) = 45
  Orthogonal (Petersen edges): 15 = E(K(5,2))
  Non-orthogonal: 30
    Obtuse (+1): 20
    Acute (-1): 10

  NOTE: obtuse = acute = 20. This is because for A_4,
  the number of root pairs with <α,β>=+1 equals those with <α,β>=-1.
  (The involution α→-α swaps obtuse and acute.)

